PaymentRails_ConfigureToken
├── when caller is not the owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
├── when token is zero address
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_ZeroTokenAddress
├── given actionType is empty string
│   ├── when actionModule is not zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_NoneActionRequiresZeroModule
│   └── when actionModule is zero address
│       ├── it should store the cleared configuration
│       └── it should emit TokenConfigured
├── given actionType is not empty
│   ├── when actionModule is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_ZeroModuleAddress
│   ├── when actionModule has no code (EOA)
│   │   └── it should revert (Solidity extcodesize check)
│   ├── when actionModule reverts on moduleType()
│   │   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_ModuleValidationFailed
│   ├── when actionModule returns empty moduleType
│   │   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_InvalidModule
│   └── when all parameters are valid
│       ├── it should store the token configuration
│       ├── it should set enabled correctly
│       ├── it should emit TokenConfigured
│       ├── when reconfiguring an existing token
│       │   ├── it should overwrite the previous configuration
│       │   └── it should emit TokenConfigured with new values
│       ├── when clearing a previously configured token
│       │   ├── it should reset config to defaults
│       │   └── it should block subsequent execution
│       └── when configuring multiple tokens
│           └── it should store independent configs
└── fuzz
    └── when minBalance is arbitrary
        └── it should store the exact minBalance value
